The admin dashboard maps weren't rendering because `admin.html` never loaded the Google Maps JavaScript API, despite `admin.js` containing all the map initialization code.

## Changes

- **Added Google Maps API loader script to `admin.html`**
  - Placed after `config.js` to ensure API key is available
  - Validates API key exists and is non-empty before loading
  - Includes error handler for load failures
  - Matches loading pattern from `script.js` (async + defer)

```html
<script src="config.js"></script>

<script>
    if (CONFIG.googleMaps && CONFIG.googleMaps.apiKey && CONFIG.googleMaps.apiKey.trim()) {
        const script = document.createElement('script');
        const apiKey = CONFIG.googleMaps.apiKey.trim();
        script.src = `https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/js?key=${apiKey}&libraries=places`;
        script.async = true;
        script.defer = true;
        script.onerror = function() {
            console.error('Failed to load Google Maps API. Please check your API key and network connection.');
        };
        document.head.appendChild(script);
    }
</script>

<script src="admin.js"></script>
```

The existing map rendering code in `admin.js` (lines 670-1042) already handles the Google Maps API correctly with proper checks for `window.google`, so no changes needed there.

## Screenshot

![Admin Dashboard](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2b659d3e-0f8e-4c3a-a4b4-a0e65807e8ad)

With this fix, quote details will display interactive route maps for each trip day showing directions from pickup through all dropoffs, as documented in the README.

